# Keep it simple

Solve the request with the smallest change that works. Do not add layers, options, abstractions, or files the current task does not need.

Before editing, read the code you will touch and restate the change in one sentence. If that sentence needs a new framework, a new pattern, or a "for later" hook, cut it back and do the direct thing.

Build every behavior with the `tdd` skill: one failing test, then only enough code to pass it, then the next slice. No production code without a failing test first.

After the change, re-read the diff and run the new test. Leave it only when the test fails first, passes after, and the diff contains nothing extra.

```text
Request: remember the last opened note
Do:     one test for "reopen shows the last note", then the few lines that store and read it
Skip:   a storage interface, a plugin system, and settings for future backends
```
